  "body": "There needs to be a link somewhere that lets you press it and your URL will change to be the corresponding URL for the current commit snapshot. (The hotkey `y` should also trigger this, like on GitHub.) This should happen in-place, not causing a reload or losing your location hash. It should automatically cause the banner from #221 to appear. It should work both when you are on \"master\" and on a branch.\n\nThe hard part here will be getting the metadata into the document for what the current commit is. Perhaps the way to do this is to write a file nearby and retrieve it with XHR.\n",
